quest.rosesword.starter.name=§p§eRose§r Tools
quest.rosesword.starter.desc=§+§p§eRose§- Tools adds a new tier of tools with unique effects. §+§8Click the §-❌§+§8 to confirm.§-
quest.rosesword.rose.name=Roses
quest.rosesword.rose.desc=First you must collect roses, they are abundant in many biomes. §8Simply have the roses in your inventory and click "Submit" to proceed.§r
quest.rosesword.algae.name=Algae
quest.rosesword.algae.desc=An often overlooked block, algae is common in hot biomes like the rainforest. Collect it using shears or silk touch. §8You can use bonemeal on them after placing them on water to produce more.§r
quest.rosesword.steel.name=Steel
quest.rosesword.steel.desc=Steel is the final ingredient required for §p§eRose§r tools.
quest.rosesword.pickaxe.name=§p§eRose§r Pickaxe
quest.rosesword.pickaxe.desc=A special pickaxe which mines slowly but has the effect of veinminer on ores and moss.
quest.rosesword.axe.name=§p§eRose§r Axe
quest.rosesword.axe.desc=A special axe which has the effect of treecapitator.
quest.rosesword.sword.name=§p§eRose§r Sword
quest.rosesword.sword.desc=A special sword which has a lifesteal effect.
quest.rosesword.helmet.name=§p§eRose§r Helmet
quest.rosesword.helmet.desc=All rose tier amour have high falling protection.
quest.rosesword.chestplate.name=§p§eRose§r Chestplate
quest.rosesword.chestplate.desc=All rose tier amour have high falling protection.
quest.rosesword.pants.name=§p§eRose§r Leggings
quest.rosesword.pants.desc=All rose tier amour have high falling protection.
quest.rosesword.boots.name=§p§eRose§r Boots
quest.rosesword.boots.desc=All rose tier amour have high falling protection.
quest.campatibility.welcome.name=Install more mods!
quest.campatibility.welcome.desc=No compatible mods found for quests ☹! Consider installing mods such as Signal Industries, Rose Tools, Better than Fishing.
quest.btf.begin.name=Fishing Expanded!
quest.btf.begin.desc=§+ Better than Fishing adds in many varieties of fish and fish accessories. These questlines will challenge you to catch and obtain them all. §+§8Click the §-❌§+§8 to confirm.§-
quest.btf.rodUpgradeIron.name=Tools of the trade
quest.btf.rodUpgradeIron.desc=Try out the Iron Fishing Rod! Trade in a §+§ofull durability§- Fishing Rod for an upgrade! Supposedly you can bait an iron fishing rod, somehow.. You also get a weird clump!
quest.btf.rodUpgradeGold.name=Gilded Rod
quest.btf.rodUpgradeGold.desc=A golden rod which grants extra chance at a lucky cast. Hold one in your inventory for a nice reward, it wont be consumed!
quest.btf.rodUpgradeDiamond.name=Dual Wield
quest.btf.rodUpgradeDiamond.desc=Sparkles! Has a chance to catch double.
quest.btf.rodUpgradeSteel.name=Reinforced Rod
quest.btf.rodUpgradeSteel.desc=Faint scuffs and wear on the dull metal of this rod tell the tale of a storied fisher. Highly durable.
quest.btf.rodUpgradeIridescent.name=Fight fire with fire
quest.btf.rodUpgradeIridescent.desc=Obtain an Iridescite Fishing Rod by any means.
quest.btf.equipped.name=Equipped
quest.btf.equipped.desc=Obtain every Iridescite tool. For bragging rights.
quest.btf.fullSet.name=Full Set
quest.btf.fullSet.desc=Obtain every Iridescite armour piece. For bragging rights.
quest.btf.allTheFishium.name=All The Fishium
quest.btf.allTheFishium.desc=Put all your fishing skill to good use and submit one of each fish for powerful rewards!
quest.btf.bootfishMaster.name=Boot-Fish Mastery
quest.btf.bootfishMaster.desc=Searching the archives.. can't find much on this guy, but ain't it cute. Obtain 8 of this mysterious mackerel.
quest.btf.herringMaster.name=Herring Mastery
quest.btf.herringMaster.desc=Silvery-coloured fish found in shallow, temperate waters. Obtain 8 of them, though avoid the red ones.
quest.btf.redMulletMaster.name=Red Mullet Mastery
quest.btf.redMulletMaster.desc=A type of goatfish (not a true mullet). Strikingly beautiful and up to 40cm. They like worms. Obtain 8 of them.
quest.btf.halibutMaster.name=Halibut Mastery
quest.btf.halibutMaster.desc=A type of flounder, this mischievous flatfish is common. Obtain 8 of them.
quest.btf.knifefishMaster.name=Knifefish Mastery
quest.btf.knifefishMaster.desc=Knifefish describes a variety of fish, though this one appears to be a featherback. Obtain 8 of them.
quest.btf.anchovyMaster.name=Anchovy Mastery
quest.btf.anchovyMaster.desc=Small common fish mostly restricted to marine waters. Oily! Obtain 8 of them.
quest.btf.goldenCarpMaster.name= Golden Carp Mastery
quest.btf.goldenCarpMaster.desc=Huge beautiful fish. May or may not be related to the gold fish. Obtain 8 of them.
quest.btf.sardineMaster.name=Sardine Mastery
quest.btf.sardineMaster.desc=Small oily fish, actually a type of herring! 8 would fit nicely in a tin.
quest.btf.rockfishMaster.name=Rockfish Mastery
quest.btf.rockfishMaster.desc=..this one is literally just a rock. Obtain 8.
quest.btf.perchMaster.name=Perch Mastery
quest.btf.perchMaster.desc=Common freshwater fish. This one looks huge! Obtain 8 of them
quest.btf.troutMaster.name=Trout Mastery
quest.btf.troutMaster.desc=Variety of species of carnivorous freshwater fish. Obtain 8 of them.
quest.btf.sunfishMaster.name=Mola Mola Mastery
quest.btf.sunfishMaster.desc=The sunfish, also known as the Mola is a large ray-finned ocean fish. Obtain 8 of them, please!
quest.btf.tunaMaster.name=Tuna Mastery
quest.btf.tunaMaster.desc=Saltwater fish. Delicious! Obtain 8 of them.
quest.btf.seaBassMaster.name=Sea Bass Mastery
quest.btf.seaBassMaster.desc=Variety of marine fish. Probably delicious! Obtain 8 of them.
quest.btf.eelMaster.name=Eel Mastery
quest.btf.eelMaster.desc=Slippery and elogated creature of the sea. Obtain 8 of these elusive animals.
quest.btf.crabMaster.name=Crab Mastery
quest.btf.crabMaster.desc=Not a fish, a crustacean yet it is here too. 2 whole families please!
quest.stardew.starter.name=§+§8§- Stardew Adventure §+§8§-
quest.stardew.starter.desc=Stardew Farming expands farming, fishing, and cooking. These questlines will challenge you to master all three. §+§8Click the §-❌§+§8 to confirm.§-
quest.stardew.cookingMaster.name=§+§8⭐§- Master Chef §+§8⭐§-
quest.stardew.cookingMaster.desc=Combine your crop and fish husbandry and dish up every type of prepared food.
quest.stardew.fishingMaster.name=§+§8⭐§- Master Fisher §+§8⭐§-
quest.stardew.fishingMaster.desc=Catch and release all the special types of fish!
quest.stardew.farmingMaster.name=§+§8⭐§- Master Farmer §+§8⭐§-
quest.stardew.farmingMaster.desc=Reap what you sow! Deliver every type of crop.
quest.stardew.totalMaster.name=§+§1§p⭐§- Total Mastery §+§1§p⭐§-
quest.stardew.totalMaster.desc=You are The Stardew!
quest.stardew.fishing.name=Pisciculture
quest.stardew.fishing.desc=Expanded fishing! Upgrade through the tiers of rods or just get right to fishin'! Heres an old rod to get you started.
quest.stardew.farming.name=Agriculture
quest.stardew.farming.desc=Smash bushes which generate naturally to obtain seeds. Have a watering can to get you started.
quest.stardew.salmon.name=Search for Salmon
quest.stardew.salmon.desc=Freshwater fish which also happens to be delicious! Obtain 8 of them
quest.stardew.bass.name=Bass Pro
quest.stardew.bass.desc=Common name for a type of ray-finned fish. Obtain 8 of them
quest.stardew.snapper.name=Oh Snap
quest.stardew.snapper.desc=Despite the name, it doesn't bite. This tropic fish inhabits warm regions. Obtain 8 of them.
quest.stardew.carrot.name=Orange you glad I didn't say Carrot
quest.stardew.carrot.desc=A sturdy and healthy root vegetable. Can be used to make vegetable stew.
quest.stardew.potato.name=Potato Potato
quest.stardew.potato.desc=New world root vegetable. A good source of starch and can be used for vegetable stew.
quest.stardew.corn.name=Also known as Maize
quest.stardew.corn.desc=Tall stout grass that produces grains. Can be combined with honey and sugar to make wax.
quest.stardew.berry.name=Berry Bonanza
quest.stardew.berry.desc=Collect every type of berry! Grape seeds can be grown by placing a stick on farmland to create a trellis.
quest.stardew.tomato.name=Tomato Tomato
quest.stardew.tomato.desc=Technically a berry!
quest.stardew.strawberry.name=Starberry
quest.stardew.strawberry.desc=Not actually a berry! This small sweet fruit is a great summer snack and can be used for fruit salad, jam, or cake.
quest.stardew.wateringCanUpgrade.name=Industrial equipment
quest.stardew.wateringCanUpgrade.desc=Show me a Steel Watering Can and click submit for some magic beans!
quest.stardew.rodUpgradeIron.name=Getting an upgrade 
quest.stardew.rodUpgradeIron.desc=A tough line with higher durability than a stone rod.
quest.stardew.rodUpgradeGold.name=Gilden an upgrade §+§4§-
quest.stardew.rodUpgradeGold.desc=A magical line seems to glisten in the water. Slightly less durabable than an iron rod.
quest.stardew.rodUpgradeDiamond.name=Bejewelling an upgrade §+§3§-
quest.stardew.rodUpgradeDiamond.desc=Diamond encrusting increase catchrates, somehow.
quest.stardew.rodUpgradeSteel.name=Steeling an upgrade §+§f§-
quest.stardew.rodUpgradeSteel.desc=A sturdy line with insane durability.

item.campatibility.tool.paxel.rose.name=§e§pRose§r Paxel
item.campatibility.tool.paxel.rose.desc=Covered in vines and moss. Has many uses.
item.campatibility.tool.paxel.iridescite.name=Iridescite Paxel
item.campatibility.tool.paxel.iridescite.desc=It seems to glisten a watery sheen even in the driest of biomes.
item.campatibility.tool.paxel.superheated_steel.name=Superheated Steel Paxel
item.campatibility.tool.paxel.superheated_steel.desc=Scorch it all with this unstable tool.
